// Digital items for sale from data/ (empty): first-party projects make their products in the Studio like every creator
// (owner, 2026-10-21; docs/decisions.md), so this list stays empty unless the owner decides otherwise. The pipeline is
// kept: an entry here gets a page at /shop/<id> (generated by scripts/build.js) and is synced into the store database
// (db/catalog.sql, same build), which is where checkout reads the price; one removed from here is unpublished there.
// Paid files and preview clips are uploaded in the admin page (/admin), never committed.
// Fields:
//   id: lowercase-hyphenated, the page address and the product's permanent key. Never change it once published.
//   title, description (plain text), type: a key of data/product-types.js. price: number in SITE.currency (0 = free).
//   tags: optional list of short lowercase words. featured: shown on the home page.
//   facets: optional structured details from the store's vocabulary (server/discovery/vocabulary.js), used by the
//     store's filters, search and recommendations: { genre, style, mood, energy, use, contents, format, daw, plugin, key,
//     os, skill } as lists of values or plain words ("WAV", "one-shots"; synonyms are folded). Only fields that apply to
//     the product's type count. Without genre, a product takes its project's genres. Only what is true of the files.
//   specs: optional { sampleRate, bitDepth } for audio. bpm: optional [min, max] (or one number) for tempo-based kinds.
//   released: optional "YYYY-MM-DD" it came out (else when it first reached the store); drives "Recently added".
//   image: optional artwork { src, width, height, alt }; without it the cover is generated from `hue` (green or purple).
//   release: optional slug of a release of the same project (made in the Studio's Music editor). includes: optional list of what's inside (plain text).
//   preview: optional { file, label }: an audio clip uploaded in the admin, played from /media/previews/<file>.
//     Never the paid file itself. metadata: optional facts shown on the product page ({ "Format": "WAV 24-bit" }).
//   project: id of the project that created it (data/projects.js); shown as "by <name>". Required.
//   pacs: optional list of Pac ids (data/pacs.js, same project) the product delivers; uploaded files are tagged with them.
//   draft: true = placeholder, not for sale. Still shown in the shop as "Coming soon", kept out of search and
//     unbuyable at checkout. Remove it once the product, price and files are real.
window.PRODUCTS = [];
